From: NAPI loop <noreply@local>
Date: Thu, 23 Oct 2026 23:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] configs: napi-c: raise PHY autoneg timeout for cold-boot loop detect

On a passive single-port Ethernet loopback the PHY autonegotiates against
its own reflected link pulses, which on a cold start takes ~12-13s to bring
the link up (observed in Linux: "end0: Link is Up" at ~13s). U-Boot's
default CONFIG_PHY_ANEG_TIMEOUT is 4000ms, so eth_init() in `loopdetect`
times out with the link still down and reports no loopback -> the board
wrongly boots the SD instead of the internal flash on cold power-on. (A warm
`reboot` kept the PHY linked, which is why it was intermittent.)

Raise the timeout to 20000ms so eth_init() waits for the slow loopback link
to come up before loopdetect probes. Trade-off: when no loopback is present
the link never comes up and this adds up to ~15s to the (SD) boot.
---
diff --git a/configs/napi-c-rk3308_defconfig b/configs/napi-c-rk3308_defconfig
--- a/configs/napi-c-rk3308_defconfig
+++ b/configs/napi-c-rk3308_defconfig
@@ -75,3 +75,4 @@
 CONFIG_CMD_NAPI_LOOPDETECT=y
 CONFIG_USE_PREBOOT=y
 CONFIG_PREBOOT="loopdetect; if test \"${napi_loop}\" = 1; then echo NAPI loopback present: booting eMMC first; setenv boot_targets \"mmc0 mmc1 nvme scsi usb pxe dhcp spi\"; fi"
+CONFIG_PHY_ANEG_TIMEOUT=20000
